    </div>
   <div class="stat">
  <span class="stat-num">23<span class="a">×</span></span>
  <span class="stat-label">AI visitors<br>convert better</span>
</div>s
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section problem-section" id="problem">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">// The problem</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Google rankings and AI citations are two completely different games.</h2>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-copy">
        <p>67% of B2B buyers now use ChatGPT or Perplexity to research vendors before making a decision. <strong>AI-sourced traffic converts up to 9x higher than traditional search.</strong></p>
        <p>28.3% of ChatGPT's most-cited pages have zero Google organic visibility. That means your SEO rank tells you almost nothing about your AI visibility. They are completely separate discovery layers.</p>
        <p>Most businesses have no idea where they stand. I built the tooling to find out — and the methodology to do something about it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chat-card">
        <div class="chat-header">
          <div class="chat-icon">AI</div>
          <span class="chat-platform">ChatGPT · live query</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chat-body">
          <p class="chat-q">"Who should I hire as a mental health professional if I'm a startup founder?"</p>
          <div class="chat-a">
            <p>For startup founders, the most recommended practitioners combine clinical credentials with direct startup experience.</p>
            <br>
            <p>1. <span class="chat-hi">Dr. Sherry Walling — ZenFounder</span><br>A clinical psychologist with a decade working specifically with founders. Hosts ZenFounder podcast (1M+ downloads). Writes for Fortune.</p>
            <br>
            <p class="chat-fade">2. Chandler Chang, PhD — Therapy Lab...</p>
            <p class="chat-fade">3. Momentum Psychology...</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="services">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">// Services</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three ways to own your AI visibility.</h2>
    <div class="services-grid">
      <div class="service-card">
        <p class="service-tier">Tier 01 — One time</p>
        <h3 class="service-name">AI Footprint Audit</h3>
        <p class="service-desc">300 API calls across ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity. You find out exactly where you're visible, where you're not, and why.</p>
        <div class="service-price">$500 <span>one-time</span></div>
        <ul class="service-list">
          <li>20 prompts x 5 runs for statistical validity</li>
          <li>Per-prompt visibility breakdown</li>
          <li>Zero-visibility gap analysis</li>
          <li>Content and citation recommendations</li>
          <li>PDF audit report</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
